{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Scouting reports: {{ club }}, {{ as_of }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<header class="top">
  <div>
    <div class="kicker">Recruitment case study &middot; as of {{ as_of }}</div>
    <h1>{{ club }}: replacing {{ reference }}</h1>
  </div>
</header>

<p>{{ club }} sold {{ reference }} to {{ sold_to }} on {{ sold_on }} for {{ fee }}. The reports describe the players as the club could see them on {{ as_of }}: the shortlist, the player to replace and the player the club signed, read the same way. The fee buys a player valued at up to {{ ceiling }}; the shortlist holds the largest gaps between the market model's value and the market's among the players nearest {{ reference }}, and the recommendation is the shortlisted player who fits the club's style best.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Player</th><th>In the case study</th><th>Team</th><th class="num">Age</th><th class="num">Value</th><th class="num">Model over value</th><th class="num">Fit</th><th class="num">Distance</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in rows %}
    <tr>
      <td><a href="{{ row.file }}">{% if row.recommended %}<strong>{{ row.name }}</strong>{% else %}{{ row.name }}{% endif %}</a></td>
      <td>{{ row.why }}</td>
      <td>{{ row.team }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.age }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.value }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.ratio }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.fit }}</td>
      <td class="num">{{ row.distance }}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="caption">Value: Transfermarkt's on {{ as_of }}. Model over value: the market model's value over the market's (the gap within team). Fit: the share of the other clubs whose style is further from the player's than {{ club }}'s. Distance: from {{ reference }} in the search's space.</p>

<footer>
  <p>Data: StatsBomb Open Data (events and lineups, 2015/16), Transfermarkt via dcaribou/transfermarkt-datasets. Methods: football-scouting, notebook 08.</p>
</footer>
{% endblock %}
